# Copy to .env.local and adjust if needed. Only used by the Vite dev server (npm run dev) to reach
# a locally-running backend (dotnet run in backend/Api, see Properties/launchSettings.json) — the
# browser talks to it directly (not proxied) so Windows Auth's Negotiate handshake works natively.
#
# Nothing else needs configuring anymore: SQL Server auth is Windows Integrated (Trusted_Connection,
# same as local dev — the IIS app pool identity just needs the right SQL permissions), and the
# TRM-RH-ADM group is already a real value in backend/Api/appsettings.json's HrGroup section. No
# Entra ID app registrations, client secrets, or per-environment IDs needed at all.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5211
